  <published>2022-02-10T14:14:19+00:00</published>
  <updated>2026-04-28T22:08:57+00:00</updated>
  <media:group>
   <media:title>Deconstructed Floral Wreath</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/N_mgD7VPKUU?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/N_mgD7VPKUU/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>You can make a floral wreath using the exact flowers you want! It's so easy! Start with a simple wreath form, like a grapevine wreath form, or a foam wreath form. Next, choose floral stems and bushes that you love! You can stick with a monochromatic color palette, all one kind of bloom, various shades of the same bloom, or just a variety of interesting shapes &amp; textures. The key to getting this densely packed look is to choose stems and bushes that have blooms in roughly the same size and shape. Next, use wire cutters to cut the heads off the flowers. Glue them on to your form using hot glue! Fill in bare spots with small leaves, and your wreath is complete!</media:description>
